Author: Duane Moore <duane.moore@ieee.org>
Date:   Mon Jul 13 22:55:24 2026 -0400

    Perf: scoped recompute for analyst-workbook live edits (#1)
    
    * Perf + correctness for analyst-workbook live edits
    
    - Model::recompute_target_cells: public cone-scoped recompute (demand-driven,
      warm-start, honors iterative calc) for driver-edit -> display-range refresh
    - Model::evaluate_formulas_only / evaluate_data_tables_only: phase split so
      callers can own the data-table policy (Excel calcMode=autoNoTable)
    - calc_results_converged: stable non-numeric target pairs now count as
      converged (mixed target sets no longer force iterate_count passes)
    - YEARFRAC: swap reversed dates before 30/360 day adjustments (Excel
      semantics; |result| is not equivalent because the day-31 rules are
      asymmetric) + regression test
    - IRONCALC_TRACE=1 instrumentation: per-pass sweep/snapshot/drift, per-table
      scenario/settle timing, recompute pass counts; per-sheet eval counters via
      Model::eval_counting_start/take. No overhead when disabled.
    
    Measured on a 45-sheet analyst model (see baba
    docs/prototypes/workbook-recompute-harness/PERF.md): full evaluate ~35s ->
    38ms per driver edit, bit-exact vs the full iterative sweep.
    
    * Quote sheet names by allow-list, not block-list
    
    A sheet name may contain any character except \ / ? * [ ] : - the old
    block-list missed '!', '&', '=', '%', and more, so re-stringified formulas
    referencing sheets like '!CAP' or 'SUMM_P&L' (real names in an analyst
    workbook) lost their quotes and could not be re-parsed (#ERROR!/#NAME?).
    Quoting is always legal, so only names matching the unquoted-identifier
    grammar (letter/_ then letters/digits/_/.) may skip quotes.
    
    Adds regression tests incl. an end-to-end evaluate through '!CAP' and
    'SUMM_P&L' references.
    
    * Add BRANCH_NOTES.md: change inventory + main-vs-data-tables-impl dependency map
    
    * Trim BRANCH_NOTES.md to upstream-candidate fixes only
    
    The data-tables-impl-specific inventory is now covered by PR #1
    (perf-scoped-recompute -> data-tables-impl); keep only the two
    fixes (YEARFRAC swap, sheet-name quoting allow-list) that are
    independent of data-tables-impl and worth an immediate upstream PR.

